course: dictionary
lesson: 11840
title: Blindfolded: eyes covered
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Blindfolded means your eyes are covered with a cloth or band, so you cannot see. «The players were blindfolded for pin the tail on the donkey.» The game tells you the clue: you have to guess where to stick the tail without looking.
explain: Blindfolded is also the past form of the verb blindfold, which means to cover someone's eyes like this. «Mum blindfolded my brother before the surprise.» Here the covering happened earlier, so it is in the past.
explain: Sometimes blindfolded is used in a saying. «I could do it blindfolded» does not mean you really wear a cloth. It means the job is so easy that you would not need your eyes. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Blindfolded means with a cloth or band over your eyes so you cannot see.
fact: Blindfold is a verb: to cover someone's eyes like this. Blindfolded is its past form.
fact: Children play blindfolded in games like pin the tail on the donkey and blind man's buff.
fact: In science, taste and touch tests are often done blindfolded to make the test fair.
fact: «I could do it blindfolded» means it is very easy for me.
exercise: «The players were blindfolded for the game of pin the tail on the donkey.» What does blindfolded mean? | Running very fast | With a hat on the head | *With a cloth over the eyes so you cannot see | Wearing a bright red coat
exercise: «Tom was blindfolded, so he could not see which fruit he was tasting.» What does blindfolded tell you? | He was eating very fast | *His eyes were covered | He had a bad cold | He was laughing and happy
exercise: Ella says, «I could tie my shoelaces blindfolded!» What does she mean? | She cannot see her own feet | Her shoelaces are very long | *Tying them would be very easy for her | She must wear a blindfold to tie them
test: In science, the taste test was done blindfolded to make it fair. Why? | *So no one could see what they were tasting | Because the food was too hot | To make the test take longer | To hide the food from the teacher
test: Blindfolded is the past form of which word? | *blindfold | blind | blindfolding | bland
exam: «The prisoners in the story were blindfolded and led across the courtyard.» What does blindfolded mean here? | *Had their eyes covered so they could not see | Given a new pair of shoes | Singing a happy song | Sitting very still in a circle
